  abstract = {Detecting public sentiment drift is a challenging task due to sentiment change over time.Existing methods first build a classification model using historical data and subsequently detect drift if the model performs much worse on new data.In this paper, we focus on distribution learning by proposing a novel Hierarchical Variational Auto-Encoder (HVAE) model to learn better distribution representation, and design a new drift measure to directly evaluate distribution changes between historical data and new data.Our experimental results demonstrate that our proposed model achieves better results than three existing state-of-theart methods.},
}

